# E §5 step 1, C-4's clause on a removal (tally 2.3, #247; review of G1, Q3): a1 makes the hole-day instance's
# `when` false, which changes it, so a binding over `adjustments` that could hold the adjustment is the hole.
# Before: 0, where pins 18 and 19 give 1 (-100.00 PLN) and 20 to 22 give 0.
=== m.tally
model f8
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-10
  start 2026-03-01
  end 2026-06-30
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input other: money PLN
input w: date
input d_at: date
input flag: bool
move pay: transfers
  on w
  at d_at
  when flag
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  d_at = 2026-03-01 "s"
  other = 1.00 PLN "s"
  opening[konto] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"
version a0
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "s"
  flag = true "s"
  w = window(2026-03-18, 2026-03-22) "s"
version a1
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-03-20
  replace flag = false "s"
ask adj: count(a in adjustments over 2026-03 .. 2026-04)
ask adj_p18: count(a in adjustments over 2026-03 .. 2026-04) with w = 2026-03-18
ask adj_p20: count(a in adjustments over 2026-03 .. 2026-04) with w = 2026-03-20
ask asum: sum(a.change for a in adjustments over 2026-03 .. 2026-04)
ask asum_p19: sum(a.change for a in adjustments over 2026-03 .. 2026-04) with w = 2026-03-19
ask k19: count(a in adjustments over 2026-03 .. 2026-04) as known 2026-03-19
=== expect
adj: ?"date within window(2026-03-18, 2026-03-22) not precise enough for the day of pay" (w)
  unknown day: w
  cut 2026-06-10
adj_p18: 1
  pinned: w = 2026-03-18
  cut 2026-06-10
adj_p20: 0
  cut 2026-06-10
asum: ?"date within window(2026-03-18, 2026-03-22) not precise enough for the day of pay" (w)
  unknown day: w
  cut 2026-06-10
asum_p19: -100.00 PLN
  pinned: w = 2026-03-19
  cut 2026-06-10
k19: 0
  cut 2026-03-19
warning: WARN-UNREAD input other is read by nothing
